<weaponBlueprint name="LEAH_WEAPON_BEAM_HARDSCIFI_OLD">
	<type>BEAM</type>
	<title>Old Laser Beam</title>
	<short>Old L. Beam</short>
	<tip>tip_beam</tip>
	<desc>A very realistic Beam that obeys REAL SCIENCE. And it's actually a Laser! Lasers don't shoot projectiles in real life, like what the hell. That doesn't even make sense. Why are Lasers and Beams separate weapons, lasers should be called plasma or something because that's what they really are. And why are beams impacted by shields? If beams are lasers and lasers are light shouldn't they be able to go through shields perfectly fine? It's not like shields are that opaque, I mean you can see through them almost perfectly, it literally makes no sense why is it like this, people really need to stop avoiding the question and just fix this obvious mistake, sheesh.</desc>
	<tooltip>Large beam that does 1 damage per room.</tooltip>
	<damage>1</damage>
	<sysDamage>1</sysDamage>
